 34AL    9BE(40AR,34ALG)               2017HA23                  ENSDF    202609
 34AL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34AL c  2017Ha23: a 69.2-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar primary beam was produced by the  
 34AL2c  Sector Focusing Cyclotron and Separated Sector Cyclotron at the Heavy  
 34AL3c  Ion Research Facility in Lanzhou (HIRFL). The secondary beam containing
 34AL4c  {+34}Al was produced via the projectile fragmentation of {+40}Ca       
 34AL5c  impinging on a 182.6-mg/cm2 {+9}Be target and was selected using       
 34AL6c  |DE-tof-B|r by the Radioactive Ion Beam Line in Lanzhou (RIBLL). The   
 34AL7c  secondary beam ions were transported into a target chamber filled with 
 34AL8c  low-temperature nitrogen and implanted into a 1500-μm-thick DSSD       
 34AL9c  sandwiched between two 3000-μm-thick plastic scintillators for beam    
 34ALAc  diagnostics and veto, respectively. The downstream scintillator also   
 34ALBc  provided fast timing signals for |b detection. |g rays were detected   
 34ALCc  using two Ge clover detectors and the fast timing signals of the |g    
 34ALDc  rays was provided by a lanthanum bromide (LaBr3) detector. Neutrons    
 34ALEc  were detected using two plastic scintillator arrays. Measured          
 34ALFc  implant-|b correlation, E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, and |g|g-coin. Deduced    
 34ALGc  levels, J, |p, decay branching ratios, log {Ift}, parent {+34}Al and   
 34ALHc  {+34}Al isomer T{-1/2}. Comparisons with shell model calculations using
 34ALIc  Gogny D1S and SDPF-M interactions.                                     
 34AL cL E,J$from the Adopted Levels.                                           
 34AL  L 0            (4-)             51.5 MS   9                              
 34AL cL T$from fitting implant-|b-929|g decay curve (2017Ha23).                
 34AL  L 46.6         (1+)             21.6 MS   15                             
 34AL cL T$from fitting implant-|b-1193|g decay curve in {+34}Si (2017Ha23). A  
 34AL2cL total of 6.5×10^5 46.6-keV isomer decay events were observed in        
 34AL3cL 2017Ha23 from fitting the inclusive |b decay curve.                    

